cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Ledgerkeep in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Ledgerkeep: A Guardrailed Autonomous Operations Agent as a Decentralized AI Service"
abstract: >-
  Ledgerkeep is a guardrailed autonomous operations agent published as a
  decentralized AI service on the ASI / Fetch.ai stack. Given a typed
  marketplace request it detects a settled-revenue anomaly by trailing z-score,
  attributes it to a specific configuration change, quantifies the loss in
  currency, and proposes the one-line fix, returning an audit object with every
  call so a caller can verify the chain from a number moved to a proposed fix.
  The agent proposes but never executes: the merge stays with a human. Its
  autonomy is bounded by named guardrails tested independently of any model,
  and it runs its full loop offline against a fixture ledger with no network.
type: software
